        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dry cough for approximately 10–12 days in total. Began with sore throat, rhinorrhoea and low-grade fevers, all of which have resolved. Cough is worse in the evening and with talking in class. On some nights it wakes the patient 1–2 times; most nights the patient sleeps through."
      }
